Imports:
  - Types:
      - Trade
      - Order
      - PairLocks
    From: freqtrade/persistence
  - Types:
      - DataProvider
    From: freqtrade/data
  - Types:
      - timeframe_to_minutes
    From: freqtrade/exchange

Usages:
  lifecycle_hooks: |
    A concrete strategy is a subclass of `IStrategy` that overrides some subset of its
    lifecycle hooks (populate_indicators, populate_entry_trend, populate_exit_trend,
    custom_stoploss, custom_exit, confirm_trade_entry, confirm_trade_exit, ...). Every
    hook has a safe default in the base class, so a minimal strategy only needs the three
    populate_* methods.

Annotations: |
  This cell defines the strategy contract every trading strategy in freqtrade implements:
  indicator/signal population, entry/exit decisions, and the optional per-trade risk-management
  callbacks the engine (backtesting or live) invokes. It builds on the trading domain model
  (`Trade`, `Order`, `PairLocks`), market data access (`DataProvider`), and timeframe
  arithmetic (`timeframe_to_minutes`).

  Use `lifecycle_hooks` when documenting or implementing a concrete strategy against this cell.

---

"HyperStrategyMixin(config: dict[str, Any])":
  location: hyper.py
  annotations: |
    Adds hyperopt-parameter-space support to `IStrategy`: discovering `BaseParameter`
    attributes on the strategy class and loading/saving optimized values for them.
  methods:
    "enumerate_parameters(space: str | None) -> parameters:list[tuple[str, BaseParameter]]": |
      Yield (attribute_name, BaseParameter) pairs declared on the strategy, optionally
      filtered to one hyperopt `space` ("buy", "sell", "protection", ...).
    "ft_load_hyper_params(hyperopt: bool)": |
      Load previously optimized parameter values from the strategy's parameter file, applying
      them onto the corresponding `BaseParameter` attributes.
    "load_params_from_file() -> params:dict[str, Any]": |
      Read the raw optimized-parameters JSON for this strategy from disk.
    "get_no_optimize_params() -> params:dict[str, Any]": |
      Return the strategy's declared parameters grouped by space, for parameters not currently
      being optimized (used for CLI/API display).

"HyperStrategyMixin::IStrategy(config: dict[str, Any])":
  location: interface.py
  annotations: |
    Mandatory interface every concrete trading strategy implements. The backtesting engine and
    the live/dry-run bot both drive strategies purely through this interface.

    `config`: full runtime configuration
  properties:
    "minimal_roi -> dict[str, Any]": |
      Time-based minimum-ROI exit thresholds, set as a class attribute by the strategy.
    "stoploss -> float": |
      Fractional stoploss distance, set as a class attribute by the strategy (mandatory).
    "timeframe -> str": |
      The candle timeframe this strategy operates on, set as a class attribute.
    "dp -> DataProvider": |
      Market-data access handle, injected by the engine before the strategy is used.
    "wallets -> Any | None": |
      Wallet/balance access handle, injected by the engine before live/dry-run use.
  methods:
    "populate_indicators(dataframe: DataFrame, metadata: dict[str, Any]) -> dataframe:DataFrame": |
      Add every technical indicator the strategy's entry/exit logic depends on to `dataframe`.

      `metadata`: at minimum contains metadata["pair"]
      `dataframe`: OHLCV dataframe with indicator columns added

      Constraints:
      - Called once per candle per pair before populate_entry_trend/populate_exit_trend
    "populate_entry_trend(dataframe: DataFrame, metadata: dict[str, Any]) -> dataframe:DataFrame": |
      Mark rows where the strategy wants to open a long/short position via enter_long/
      enter_short columns.
    "populate_exit_trend(dataframe: DataFrame, metadata: dict[str, Any]) -> dataframe:DataFrame": |
      Mark rows where the strategy wants to close a position via exit_long/exit_short
      columns.
    "bot_loop_start(current_time: datetime)": |
      Called once per bot iteration, before per-pair analysis; used for state that must be
      refreshed independently of any one pair.
    "confirm_trade_entry(pair: str, order_type: str, amount: float, rate: float, time_in_force: str, current_time: datetime, entry_tag: str | None, side: str) -> allow:bool": |
      Last chance to veto an entry signal before the order is placed.

      `allow`: True to proceed with the order; default implementation always returns True
    "confirm_trade_exit(pair: str, trade: Trade, order_type: str, amount: float, rate: float, time_in_force: str, exit_reason: str, current_time: datetime) -> allow:bool": |
      Last chance to veto an exit signal before the order is placed.
    "custom_stoploss(pair: str, trade: Trade, current_time: datetime, current_rate: float, current_profit: float, after_fill: bool) -> stoploss:float | None": |
      Compute a dynamic (e.g. trailing) stoploss for an open trade.

      `stoploss`: `None` to keep the current stoploss unchanged; default returns self.stoploss
    "custom_exit(pair: str, trade: Trade, current_time: datetime, current_rate: float, current_profit: float) -> reason:str | bool | None": |
      Request a custom (non-ROI, non-stoploss) exit for an open trade.

      `reason`: exit-reason string/True to exit now, or `None`/False to keep the trade open
    "custom_stake_amount(pair: str, current_time: datetime, current_rate: float, proposed_stake: float, min_stake: float | None, max_stake: float, leverage: float, entry_tag: str | None, side: str) -> stake:float": |
      Override the position size the engine proposes for a new entry.
    "adjust_trade_position(trade: Trade, current_time: datetime, current_rate: float, current_profit: float, min_stake: float | None, max_stake: float, current_entry_rate: float, current_exit_rate: float) -> stake_delta:float | None": |
      Request a partial add-to/reduce-from an already-open position (DCA-style averaging).

      `stake_delta`: positive to add stake, negative to reduce, `None` for no adjustment
    "leverage(pair: str, current_time: datetime, current_rate: float, proposed_leverage: float, max_leverage: float, entry_tag: str | None, side: str) -> leverage:float": |
      Override the leverage the engine proposes for a new futures/margin entry.
    "informative_pairs() -> pairs:list[tuple[str, str]]": |
      Declare additional (pair, timeframe) combinations the strategy needs refreshed even
      though it doesn't trade them directly.

"BaseParameter(default: Any, space: str | None, optimize: bool, load: bool)":
  location: parameters.py
  annotations: |
    Base type for one strategy attribute exposed to hyperopt as an optimizable dimension.

    `default`: value used outside of hyperopt or when `optimize` is False
    `space`: hyperopt space this parameter belongs to ("buy", "sell", "protection", ...);
    inferred from the enclosing attribute name when omitted
    `optimize`: include this parameter in hyperopt search
    `load`: load a previously optimized value for this parameter from the params file

"BaseParameter::IntParameter(low: int, high: int | None, default: int, space: str | None, optimize: bool, load: bool)":
  location: parameters.py
  annotations: |
    Integer-valued hyperopt dimension over [low, high]. Representative of the numeric
    parameter family (RealParameter, DecimalParameter follow the same pattern with
    float/decimal-rounded values).

"BaseParameter::CategoricalParameter(categories: list[Any], default: Any | None, space: str | None, optimize: bool, load: bool)":
  location: parameters.py
  annotations: |
    Hyperopt dimension choosing among a fixed list of `categories`. BooleanParameter is a
    thin specialization fixing `categories` to [True, False].

"informative(timeframe: str, asset: str, fmt: str | None, candle_type: str | None, ffill: bool, cache: bool) -> decorator:Any":
  location: informative_decorator.py
  annotations: |
    Decorator marking a populate_indicators_<n> method as an informative-pair indicator
    populator; the engine merges its output into the main dataframe automatically.

    `timeframe`: timeframe of the informative pair to fetch
    `asset`: pair to fetch; defaults to the strategy's current pair when empty
    `ffill`: forward-fill the merged informative columns onto the base timeframe

